# Prestium 2.1 (security audit): "user" may set the clock as root only through prestium-set-clock,
# which refuses dates before the image was built (or 10 years after) and raises a safety flag.
# The old rule (sudo date -s with any date) let any unconfined program of the user move the clock
# anywhere, and an even older one (date with any arguments) allowed "date -f FILE" (GTFOBins).
#   sudo prestium-set-clock 2026-11-10 14:30
user	ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/prestium-set-clock ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}(:[0-9]{2})?$
